# Maintainer Documentation

In-source maintainer docs are a **third layer** next to the public contract and algorithm comments in `documentation-standards.mdc`. They record **why** the system is shaped this way.

| Layer | Question | Where |
|-------|----------|--------|
| **Architecture / decisions** | Why this module, package, or approach? | `package-info.java` and type-level Javadoc on support types |

## Keep Current

- When adding a module, package, agent, or simulation, update the `package-info.java` for that package in the same change
- Document decisions (for example why robots live in `robots`, how a simulation is launched) — not a restatement of the code
- Use real workspace paths and Maven execution ids
- Do not invent a parallel wiki or docs site unless asked
